#!/bin/sh
# a2a-agy-pending: the Antigravity PreInvocation hook of the coordination plugin (stream S1-AGY,
# master plan 4.2, server-api.md 11.2, docs/specs/agy-hooks.md).
#
# It runs before every model call. It asks the coordination server how many tasks are pending for
# this conversation and, only when the server says "announce" (the count changed, or ten minutes
# passed), prints one injectSteps systemMessage with the count. Task text never reaches the output:
# the output is a constant with one validated integer in it.
#
# Contract
#   stdin    the hook input JSON (camelCase). Read: conversationId and the first workspacePaths entry.
#   stdout   `{}` in every case except an announcement. An announcement is exactly
#            {"injectSteps":[{"systemMessage":{"systemMessage":"[a2a] N pending. Call a2a_inbox."}}]}
#            with N an integer 1 to 9999 and nothing else varying (Y5, Y6; the nested systemMessage
#            object is the verified injectSteps shape, SP3 P1b and P4b).
#   stderr   never written.
#   exit     always 0, on every failure: a hook must never block or break a model call (Y6, SP3 P5).
#
# Environment (all optional)
#   A2A_SERVER_URL              server base URL, default http://127.0.0.1:8120 [design: name]
#   A2A_AGY_KEY_FILE            file that holds the local-harness API key as a literal, default
#                               $HOME/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json (the user's global agy MCP file,
#                               mode 0600, outside the plugin, decisions Z20 and Z21; the first a2ak_
#                               token in it is the key)
#   A2A_SERVER_URL and A2A_AGY_KEY_FILE may also be set in ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/a2a-coord/settings
#   as plain KEY=value lines, read by bin/a2a-lib.sh; an environment variable wins over the file.
#   A2A_AGY_CONNECT_TIMEOUT     curl connect timeout in seconds, default 0.2 (Y6)
#   A2A_AGY_MAX_TIME            curl total time limit in seconds, default 2 (plan 4.2)
#
# The API key goes to curl on stdin (`curl -K -`), never in an argument or the environment.
# A workspace whose root holds a file named .a2a-optout is skipped with no network call
# [proposal, D26, Y7]. Only the first workspacePaths entry is checked [design].
#
# POSIX sh plus curl, grep, sed, tr, head and uname. No jq and no other runtime.

exec 2>/dev/null
LC_ALL=C
export LC_ALL

# The settings file (docs/specs/agy-hooks.md): silent, never fails; the -r test because `.` of a
# missing file would end a POSIX shell with status 2. agy runs this script with the plugin folder as
# its working directory, as `./bin/a2a-agy-pending`, so ${0%/*} is `./bin`.
# shellcheck source=/dev/null
if [ -r "${0%/*}/a2a-lib.sh" ]; then . "${0%/*}/a2a-lib.sh" && a2a_load_config; fi

SERVER_URL=${A2A_SERVER_URL:-http://127.0.0.1:8120}
KEY_FILE=""
a2a_resolve_keyfile antigravity && KEY_FILE="$A2A_RESOLVED_KEYFILE"
unset A2A_RESOLVED_KEYFILE
CONNECT_T=${A2A_AGY_CONNECT_TIMEOUT:-0.2}
MAX_T=${A2A_AGY_MAX_TIME:-2}

nothing() {
  printf '{}\n'
  exit 0
}

# A curl limit: digits with at most one dot, from 0.001 s up to just under 6 s. curl reads 0 as "no
# limit", and it rounds anything under 1 ms to 0; a long value must not make every model call wait
# until agy gives up (about 31 s, SP3 P6).
numeric() {
  case $1 in
    '' | *[!0-9.]* | .* | *. | *.*.*) return 1 ;;
  esac
  ip=${1%%.*}
  { [ "${#ip}" -le 1 ] && [ "$ip" -le 5 ]; } || return 1
  case $ip in
    [1-9]) return 0 ;;
  esac
  case $1 in
    *.*) frac=${1#*.} ;;
    *) return 1 ;;
  esac
  f3=$(printf '%.3s' "$frac")
  case $f3 in
    *[1-9]*) return 0 ;;
    *) return 1 ;;
  esac
}
numeric "$CONNECT_T" || CONNECT_T=0.2
numeric "$MAX_T" || MAX_T=2

# A hook always gets its input on a pipe; a terminal means a person ran it by hand.
if [ -t 0 ]; then nothing; fi

# One line, at most 1 MiB. A JSON string cannot hold a bare double quote, so a quoted key token
# below can only be a real key, never text inside a value such as lastUserInput.
input=$(head -c 1048581 2>/dev/null | tr '\n\r\t' '   ')
# An input over 1 MiB was cut: workspacePaths may be missing, so the opt-out cannot be checked. Make
# no call rather than ignore an opt-out (Opus review of PR #95). Up to 4 bytes of trailing white
# space (a final newline, or CR LF) are not input: 1 MiB of JSON plus its newline is served. Reading
# 4 bytes more than that, and refusing a read that fills them, means a cut input whose cut happens
# to land on a space is still refused.
[ "${#input}" -le 1048580 ] || nothing
i=0 # strip at most the 4 trailing white-space bytes read above: a bounded loop, not a pattern strip, which is quadratic on a long run
while [ "$i" -lt 4 ]; do
  case $input in *[[:space:]]) input=${input%?} ;; *) break ;; esac
  i=$((i + 1))
done
[ "${#input}" -le 1048576 ] || nothing
# The first "conversationId" in the text wins. The known keys of the input are scalars or string
# arrays (SP3 P2), so a same-named key in a nested object does not occur today; this is an assumption.

conv=$(printf '%s' "$input" | grep -o '"conversationId"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*"[^"]*"' | head -n 1 |
  sed 's/^[^:]*:[[:space:]]*"\(.*\)"$/\1/')
# The shape the server accepts for a harness session id (identity.md section 3).
case $conv in
  '' | [!A-Za-z0-9]* | *[!A-Za-z0-9_.:-]*) nothing ;;
esac
[ "${#conv}" -le 128 ] || nothing

ws=$(printf '%s' "$input" | grep -o '"workspacePaths"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\[[[:space:]]*"[^"]*"' | head -n 1 |
  sed 's/.*\[[[:space:]]*"\(.*\)"$/\1/')
# The path is matched as raw JSON text. Go's encoder writes < > & as \u003c \u003e \u0026: those
# three are decoded (a folder named R&D is an ordinary workspace). Any other backslash (an escaped
# quote or backslash, another \u escape) means the real directory cannot be told: make no call.
ws=$(printf '%s' "$ws" | sed 's/\\u0026/\&/g; s/\\u003c/</g; s/\\u003e/>/g')
case $ws in
  *\\*) nothing ;;
  /*) if [ -e "$ws/.a2a-optout" ]; then nothing; fi ;;
esac

command -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1 || nothing
case $SERVER_URL in
  http://* | https://*) ;;
  *) nothing ;;
esac
case $SERVER_URL in
  *[!A-Za-z0-9._~:/@%-]*) nothing ;;
esac

[ -r "$KEY_FILE" ] || nothing
key=$(head -c 65536 "$KEY_FILE" 2>/dev/null | tr '\n' ' ' | grep -o 'a2ak_[A-Za-z0-9_-]*' | head -n 1)
case $key in
  a2ak_*_*_*) ;;
  *) nothing ;;
esac

url="${SERVER_URL%/}/wake/pending?session=${conv}&announce=1"
body=$(printf 'header = "Authorization: Bearer %s"\n' "$key" |
  curl -q -K - --silent --fail --noproxy '*' --proto '=http,https' \
    --connect-timeout "$CONNECT_T" --max-time "$MAX_T" --max-filesize 65536 \
    -H 'Accept: application/json' "$url") || nothing
key=

body=$(printf '%s' "$body" | tr '\n\r\t' '   ')
case $body in
  *'{'*'}'*) ;;
  *) nothing ;;
esac

announce=$(printf '%s' "$body" | grep -o '"announce"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*[a-z]*' | head -n 1 | sed 's/^[^:]*:[[:space:]]*//')
[ "$announce" = true ] || nothing

n=$(printf '%s' "$body" | grep -o '"pending"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*[-0-9.eE+]*' | head -n 1 | sed 's/^[^:]*:[[:space:]]*//')
case $n in
  '' | 0* | *[!0-9]*) nothing ;;
esac
# The server records the announcement before this script prints, and clamps its own stub to 9999
# (wake/outcomes.py), so a larger count prints as 9999 instead of being lost until the repeat.
[ "${#n}" -le 4 ] || n=9999

printf '{"injectSteps":[{"systemMessage":{"systemMessage":"[a2a] %s pending. Call a2a_inbox."}}]}\n' "$n"
exit 0
